[{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Using the following velocity-time graph</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.65/questions/assets/diagrams/q1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>show that</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=u+at\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=\\frac12(u+v)t\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=ut+\\frac12at^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=vt-\\frac12at^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Acceleration is gradient: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{v-u}t\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow at=v-u\\Rightarrow v=u+at\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Displacement is area under curve:</p>","<p>Trapezium: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=\\frac12(u+v)t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Displacement is area under curve:</p>","<p>Rectangle + Triangle: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=ut+\\frac12t\\times(v-u)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>But <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"at=v-u\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=ut+\\frac12t\\times at=ut+\\frac12at^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Displacement is area under curve:</p>","<p>Rectangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\" data-display=\"false\"></span> Triangle: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=vt-\\frac12t\\times(v-u)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>But <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"at=v-u\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=vt-\\frac12t\\times at=vt-\\frac12at^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>By substituting <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=u+at\" data-display=\"false\"></span> into <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=vt-\\frac12at^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> show how <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v^2=u^2+2as\" data-display=\"false\"></span> may be derived.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"at=v-u\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\frac{v-u}a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=v\\left(\\frac{v-u}a\\right)-\\frac12(v-u)\\left(\\frac{v-u}a\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow as=v(v-u)-\\frac12(v-u)(v-u)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow as=v^2-uv-\\frac12v^2+uv-\\frac12u^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow as=\\frac12v^2-\\frac12u^2\\Rightarrow2as=v^2-u^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow v^2=u^2+2as\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>In each case, use the constant acceleration formulae with the given values:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2,u=4,v=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=-2,t=3,s=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=12,t=4,v=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=2,a=1.5,v=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=20,t=8,u=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6=4+2t\\Rightarrow t=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5=3u-9\\Rightarrow u=\\frac{14}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12=4\\times5-8a\\Rightarrow a=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9=4+3s\\Rightarrow s=\\frac53\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20=4(5+v)\\Rightarrow v=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=20,t=6,v=2.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, using the constant acceleration formulae, find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20=15-18a\\Rightarrow a=-\\frac5{18}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20=3(u+2.5)\\Rightarrow u=\\frac{25}6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=15,v=4.5,u=1.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, using the constant acceleration formulae, find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15=\\frac12(1.5+4.5)t\\Rightarrow t=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20.25=2.25+30a\\Rightarrow a=\\frac35\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>A particle is moving in a straight line from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with constant acceleration <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Its speed at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and it takes 7 seconds to travel between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the speed of the particle at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the distance from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=6+2\\times7=20\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=6\\times7+\\frac12\\times2\\times7^2=91\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Katie is walking along a straight path of length 100 m initially at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.1\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and has constant acceleration <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.05\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the time it takes for Katie to travel the path.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"100=1.1t+0.025t^2\\Rightarrow t=-89.0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=45.0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\ge0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so 45.0 s (3 SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Fasil is running along the road and for this part he can be modelled as running with constant acceleration of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.1\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. He is running at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when he passes a lamp post. A further 10 seconds later he passes a litter bin. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the distance between the lamp post and the litter bin.</p></li><li><p>the speed at which Fasil passes the litter bin.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=ut+\\frac12at^2=5\\times10+\\frac12\\times0.1\\times10^2=55\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=u+at=5+0.1\\times10=6\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>Find the acceleration and the displacement given each of the following scenarios, where the object starts from rest:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=4\\text{ ms}^{-1},t=3\\text{ s}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=1.4\\text{ cms}^{-1},t=2\\text{ s}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=10\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4=0+3a\\Rightarrow a=\\frac43\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=\\frac32(0+4)\\Rightarrow s=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.014=0+2a\\Rightarrow a=0.007\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=\\frac22(0+0.014)\\Rightarrow s=0.014\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10=0+at\\Rightarrow a=\\frac{10}t\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=\\frac t2(0+10)\\Rightarrow s=5t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>A cyclist is cycling on a straight flat road. Her initial velocity is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then she accelerates at a constant rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for 12 seconds before reaching a speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3u\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><p>Express <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3u=u+12a\\Rightarrow a=\\frac u6\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>In perfect conditions, it takes 38 metres to stop a car driving at a speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"80\\text{ kmh}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the time it takes to stop assuming the deceleration is constant.</p></li><li><p>Comment on why this may not be an accurate answer for modelling the stopping of a car in a real-world scenario.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=38,v=0,u=\\frac{200}9\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"38=\\frac12\\left(\\frac{200}9+0\\right)t\\Rightarrow t=\\frac{171}{50}=3.42\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Stopping times are affected by the type of vehicle, the condition of the brakes, the weather and condition of the road. Also the driver needs `thinking time' to apply the brakes.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Ceri cycles 2 km on a straight horizontal section of a race. She is cycling <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"28\\text{ kmh}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> initially and finishes the section at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"32\\text{ kmh}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><p>Find her acceleration for this section, assuming she accelerates at a constant rate.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=2000,u=\\frac{70}9,v=\\frac{80}9\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac{80}9\\right)^2=\\left(\\frac{70}9\\right)^2+4000a\\Rightarrow a=\\frac1{216}=0.00463\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>A car travels along a straight horizontal road with constant acceleration, passing three points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It takes 15 s to travel from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It is moving at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the acceleration of the car</p></li><li><p>Find the speed of the car at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given the distance between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is 150 metres.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16=12+15a\\Rightarrow a=\\frac4{15}=0.267\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12^2=u^2+2\\times\\frac4{15}\\times150\\Rightarrow u=8\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>A car is travelling along a straight horizontal road with a constant acceleration, passing three points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><p>It takes 6 seconds to travel from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and a further 4 seconds to travel 10.4 metres from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><p>It is travelling at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as it passes point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the acceleration of the car.</p></li><li><p>the speed of the car at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>how far the car travels beyond point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> before it comes to rest.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10.4=5\\times4+\\frac12\\times4^2a\\Rightarrow a=-1.2\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5=u-1.2\\times6\\Rightarrow u=12.2\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10.4=\\frac12(5+v)\\times4\\Rightarrow v=0.2\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v^2=u^2+2as\\Rightarrow0=0.2^2-2\\times1.2s\\Rightarrow s=\\frac1{60}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<p>0.0167 m (3 SF) beyond <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>A vehicle travels with constant acceleration along a straight flat road.</p><p>It passes three checkpoints <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and in each case is travelling at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"50\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the ratio of the times taken to drive the distances <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>the distance between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given the distance <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is 150 metres.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30=15+at\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"50=30+at\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{15}a:\\frac{20}a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3:4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"50^2=15^2+2\\times150a\\Rightarrow a=\\frac{91}{12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30^2=15^2+2\\times\\frac{91}{12}s\\Rightarrow s=\\frac{4050}{91}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>44.5 m (3SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>A truck is travelling along a straight horizontal road with constant acceleration.</p><p>A set of traffic lights is 25 metres away from the truck. A junction is a further 110 metres on from the traffic lights.</p><p>The truck takes 2 seconds to travel to the traffic lights and 5 seconds to travel between the traffic lights and the junction.</p><p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the acceleration of the truck.</p></li><li><p>the speed of the truck in its initial position.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Final speed of part one = Initial speed of part two</p>","<p>Part one: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25=2v-2a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Part two: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"110=5u+\\frac{25}2a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Solving simultaneously: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\frac{213}{14}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{19}7\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2.71\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25=2u+2\\times\\frac{19}7\\Rightarrow u=\\frac{137}{14}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so initial speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9.79\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>Two cars, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, are travelling along a flat, straight road.</p><p>Car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is driving at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> throughout its motion.</p><p>Initially, car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is 15 metres behind car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and is driving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.2\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> slower than car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> but is accelerating at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><p>Find the time it takes for Car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to catch up Car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>CAR A: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=ut\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>CAR B: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=-15+(u-0.2)t+\\frac12\\times0.8t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Solving simultaneously:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ut=-15+(u-0.2)t+\\frac12\\times0.8t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=-15-0.2t+0.4t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=-5.88\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=6.38\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so 6.38 seconds</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>A car is travelling on a straight flat road.</p><p>Initially it has velocity of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and drives with constant acceleration, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, past two checkpoints.</p><p>It reaches the first checkpoint which is at 48 metres from the initial point, in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the initial speed for the second phase of the motion in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>The next checkpoint is a further 204 metres away and it reaches it in 10 seconds.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>First phase: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"48=6k+\\frac12ak^2\\Rightarrow a=\\frac{96-12k}{k^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"48=\\frac12(v+6)k\\Rightarrow u=\\frac{96}k-6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"204=\\left(\\frac{96}k-6\\right)\\times10+\\frac12\\left(\\frac{96-12k}{k^2}\\right)\\times10^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"204k^2=(96k-6k^2)\\times10+50(96-12k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"204k^2=960k-60k^2+4800-600k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"264k^2-360k-4800=0\\Rightarrow k=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=-\\frac{40}{11}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>But only the positive <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives a result that fits the model. So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{96-12\\times5}{25}=1.44\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q19","number":19,"question":"<p>A stone is dropped on a planet from a height of 3 metres. It takes 2.2 seconds to hit the surface. Find the acceleration due to gravity on this planet.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3=0+\\frac12a\\times2.2^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{150}{121}=1.24\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q20","number":20,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.81\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> A ball is dropped, and it takes 0.8 seconds to reach the ground. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the height above the ground from which the ball is dropped.</p></li><li><p>the speed in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the speed when the ball hits the ground.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=0+\\frac12\\times-9.81\\times0.8^2=-3.1392\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<p>Height is 3.1392 m</p>","<p>3.14 m (3 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=-9.81t\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=9.81t\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=-9.81\\times0.8=-7.848\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7.848\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7.85\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q21","number":21,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> An object, which is initially at rest is dropped from a height of 8m above the ground.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Calculate the speed of the object when it hits the ground.</p></li><li><p>Calculate the time it takes to hit the ground.</p></li><li><p>State a refinement to the model, apart from air resistance, which would make the model more realistic.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v^2=0+2\\times9.8\\times16\\Rightarrow v=\\frac{28}5\\sqrt5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=12.5\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=13\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8=0+\\frac12\\times9.8t^2\\Rightarrow t=\\frac47\\sqrt5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1.28\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s (3 SF)</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1.3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>A more accurate value of the acceleration of gravity (including considering where on the planet the object is dropped as g is variable).</p>","<p>Calculating for the object having a shape rather than being modelled as a particle.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q22","number":22,"question":"<p>A ball is projected upwards from the ground with speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"14.7\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the time it takes to reach ground again.</p></li><li><p>the total distance travelled in the first 2 seconds of motion.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Reaches ground when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=14.7t+\\frac12\\times-9.8t^2\\Rightarrow t=0,t=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>It travels to maximum height:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v^2=u^2+2as\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=14.7^2+2\\times-9.8s\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore s=11.025\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=ut+\\frac12at^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"11.025=14.7\\times t-\\frac12\\times9.8t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore t=1.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds to reach maximum height</p>","<p>Final 0.5 seconds:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=0+\\frac12\\times9.8\\times0.5^2=1.225\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<p>So total distance is 12.25 metres</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q23","number":23,"question":"<p>A pebble is thrown upwards in the air from the edge of a bridge with a velocity of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"24.5\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the time it takes for the ball to reach its maximum height.</p></li></ol><p>After 6.5 seconds from being thrown, the pebble lands in the river below. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>the height of the bridge at the point where the pebble was thrown.</p></li><li><p>the total distance travelled by the pebble.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Max height when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=24.5-9.8t\\Rightarrow t=2.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=24.5\\times6.5+\\frac12\\times-9.8\\times6.5^2=-47.775\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So height of bridge is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=47.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m (3 SF)</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=48\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Distance to max height: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=24.5^2+2\\times-9.8s\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow s=30.625\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Total distance: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\times30.625+47.775=109.025\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<p>So distance is 109 m or 110 m (2 SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q24","number":24,"question":"<p>A stone is thrown vertically upwards in the air starting 1.65 m above the ground being projected with initial speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6.25\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The stone moves freely under gravity.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the time at which the stone hits the ground.</p></li><li><p>Find the times at which the stone is precisely 2 m above the ground.</p></li><li><p>Hence find the total time the stone spends more than 2 metres above the ground.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Hitting the ground: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=-1.65\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1.65=6.25t+\\frac12\\times-9.8t^2\\Rightarrow t=1.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=-\\frac{11}{49}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds after being thrown.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>0.35 m above the start point.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.35=6.25t+\\frac12\\times-9.8t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow t=1.2168\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.05870\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1.22\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.0587\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s (3 SF)</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.059\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.2168\\ldots-0.05870\\ldots=1.15\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds (3 SF)</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds (2 SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q25","number":25,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=10\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> A ball is thrown vertically upwards with initial speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> from a height of 15m above the ground. It hits the ground with speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"22\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the initial speed.</p></li><li><p>What is the greatest height it reaches?</p></li><li><p>Find the time it takes to hit the ground.</p></li><li><p>Given the ball should be subject to air resistance, explain the how this would affect your answers to the previous parts of the question.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"22^2=u^2+2\\times-10\\times-15\\Rightarrow u=\\pm2\\sqrt{46}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"13.6\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (1 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Greatest height when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=(2\\sqrt{46})^2+2\\times-10\\times s\\Rightarrow s=9.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So 24.2m (3 SF) above the ground</p>","<p>20 m (1 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-15=-22t+\\frac12\\times10t^2\\Rightarrow t=3.5565,t=0.8435\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=3.56\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds</p>","<p>4 s (1 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Consider reducing the acceleration due to gravity (as resistance would change the total acceleration)</p>","<p>The initial speed would be larger to give the same final speed, this would lead to a higher greatest height reached, and it would take longer to hit the ground.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q26","number":26,"question":"<p>A parachutist steps off a plane at a height of 2800 m. They free-fall for 4 seconds before opening their parachute.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the speed of the parachutist the moment the parachute opens.</p></li></ol><p>It is given that from the point the parachute opens, they decelerate at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for 3 seconds before reaching a constant speed.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Find the total time it takes to reach the ground from initially stepping off the plane.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=0-10\\times4=-40\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"40\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Phase 1:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=0\\times4+\\frac12\\times(-10)\\times4^2=-80\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so 80 m</p>","<p>Phase 2:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=-40,a=12,t=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=-40\\times3+\\frac12\\times12\\times3^2=-66\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so 66 m</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=u+at=-40+12\\times3=-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Phase 3:</p>","<p>Distance left: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2800-80-66=2654\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2654=-4t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=663.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Total time: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4+3+663.5=670.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds</p>","<p>700 s (1 SF -- AQA)</p>","<p>[Please note that the numbers used here are unrealistic due to the impact of air resistance when skydiving]</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q27","number":27,"question":"<p>A ball is thrown vertically upwards from the ground at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> whilst simultaneously a second identical ball is thrown vertically downwards at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> from a height of 10 metres above the ground. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the time at which both balls are at the same height.</p></li><li><p>the distance from the ground at which both balls are at the same height.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Ball A: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=20t-5t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Ball B: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s-10=-5t-5t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Solving simultaneously,</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20t-5t^2=-5t-5t^2+10\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25t=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=20\\times0.4-5\\times0.4^2=7.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=7\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m (1 SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q28","number":28,"question":"<p>A ball <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is thrown vertically upwards from the ground at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> whilst simultaneously a second identical ball <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is thrown vertically upwards at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> from a height of 5 metres above the ground. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the amount of time that both balls are above the height of the initial start point of ball <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>the time at which both balls are at the same height.</p></li><li><p>the distance from the ground at which both balls are at the same height.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Ball A: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=20t-5t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Ball B: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s-5=12t-5t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Ball A: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=5t^2-20t+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=2\\pm\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.2679\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=3.73\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Ball B: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=12t-5t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0,t=2.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So they are both above the height for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2.4-0.2679\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=2.13\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds</p>","<p>2 seconds (1 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Solving simultaneously,</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20t-5t^2=12t-5t^2+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8t=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\frac58=0.625\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds</p>","<p>0.6 seconds (1 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\frac58\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=20\\times\\frac58-5\\times\\left(\\frac58\\right)^2=\\frac{675}{64}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=10.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres from the ground</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m (1 SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q29","number":29,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in exact form</strong> An object is dropped from a height of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=\\sqrt{2gh}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v^2=0+2\\times-g\\times-h\\Rightarrow v=\\sqrt{2gh}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q30","number":30,"question":"<p>A stone is dropped from a height of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres above horizontal ground. It falls freely downwards. Its speed when reaching the ground is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=\\frac{32}g\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8^2=0^2-2\\times-g\\times h\\Rightarrow h=\\frac{64}{2g}=\\frac{32}g\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q31","number":31,"question":"<p>A ball is projected directly upwards at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find an expression for</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the maximum height in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the time it takes to return to its start point in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=u^2-2gs\\Rightarrow s=\\frac{u^2}{2g}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=ut-\\frac12gt^2\\Rightarrow t=\\frac{-u\\pm\\sqrt{u^2-0}}{-g}\\Rightarrow t=\\frac{u\\mp\\sqrt{u^2}}g\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So returned when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\frac{2u}g\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.65-q32","number":32,"question":"<p>Two particles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are released from rest. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is released from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres above a horizontal surface. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is released 0.5 seconds later from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{k}{10}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres above the horizontal surface. They land simultaneously on the surface at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds after the release of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\\approx0.267g\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Particle A: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-k=0-\\frac12gt^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Particle B: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac k{10}=0-\\frac12g(t-0.5)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac{\\frac12gt^2}{10}=-\\frac12g(t-0.5)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t^2=10(t-0.5)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t^2=10t^2-10t+2.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=9t^2-10t+2.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\frac{10\\pm\\sqrt{10}}{18}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.7312376\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.3798734633\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.3798734633\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is before particle B is released.</p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=0.2673542488g\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\\approx0.267g\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]}]